---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const img = 'w-full rounded-xl border border-gray-200 shadow-md';
const h2 = 'text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-3 pt-6 border-t border-gray-100';
const p = 'text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-4';
---

<Base title="MyBackHaul — how it works">
  <main class="min-h-screen bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10 sm:py-16">
      <a href="/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-blue-600 font-semibold text-sm mb-6 hover:text-blue-700">
        <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7" /></svg>
        MyBackHaul
      </a>

      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900 leading-tight mb-4">How MyBackHaul works</h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 mb-2">
        MyBackHaul matches distributors' loads with hauliers who have spare capacity on the way
        back — with a proof of delivery you can rely on, captured even where there's no signal.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>Signing in</h2>
      <p class={p}>
        Open the <a href="/app" class="text-blue-600 font-medium">driver app</a> and sign in with your
        email and password, or with Google. If your account belongs to more than one company, an
        <strong>Acting as</strong> switcher lets you choose which one you're working as — the screen
        changes to match.
      </p>
      <img src="/guide/sign-in.png" alt="The MyBackHaul sign-in screen" class={img} />

      <h2 class={h2}>For shippers — post a load</h2>
      <p class={p}>
        Fill in where the goods are collected and delivered, the consignment, the price, and the
        collection and delivery dates. Post it, and hauliers can see it straight away. MyBackHaul
        geocodes the route automatically within a minute.
      </p>
      <img src="/guide/post-a-load.png" alt="The Post a load form" class={img} />

      <h2 class={h2}>For carriers — find a backhaul</h2>
      <p class={p}>
        Browse the available loads — each shows the route, pallets, headline price, and distance.
        Accepting one makes it your current job. You never see a shipper's private details until
        you've accepted.
      </p>
      <img src="/guide/available-loads.png" alt="The Available loads browse" class={img} />

      <h2 class={h2}>For drivers — the 30-second moment</h2>
      <p class={p}>
        When you've delivered, tap <strong>Mark delivered</strong>: take a photo of the goods,
        capture the recipient's name and signature, and record it. It saves to your phone
        instantly — <strong>even with no signal</strong> — and sends itself automatically the moment
        you're back online.
      </p>
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <figure class="m-0">
          <img src="/guide/mark-delivered.png" alt="The Mark delivered screen" class={img} />
          <figcaption class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-2">Capture the proof of delivery.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="m-0">
          <img src="/guide/delivery-recorded.png" alt="The Delivery recorded confirmation" class={img} />
          <figcaption class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-2">Saved on your device, sent when you have signal.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>

      <h2 class={h2}>Works with no signal</h2>
      <p class={p}>
        Deliveries happen in loading bays and rural lay-bys where signal is patchy. MyBackHaul is
        built for that: a proof of delivery is recorded on your device the moment it happens, and
        delivered to the shipper when signal returns — nothing is ever lost.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-12">
        <a href="/app" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-blue-600 text-white px-6 py-3 rounded-lg font-semibold shadow-lg shadow-blue-600/20 hover:bg-blue-700 transition-colors">
          Open the driver app
          <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13 7l5 5m0 0l-5 5m5-5H6" /></svg>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
